{
  "id": "Cinematics",
  "name": "Cinematics (影片)",
  "notes": ["Colours are linear RGB.  In set data a colour input may name a palette entry instead of giving RGB.", "A finish is a palette colour with its roughness, metallicness and weathering: the grime that darkens it in broad patches ('grime': strength, size in metres) and the streaks that run down vertical faces ('streaks': strength, spacing in metres).", "Everything is built for EEVEE; a film's sets may override any finish parameter through their 'materials' (\"<finish>.<parameter>\" or \"color:<palette key>\").", "A module is a facade panel in unit coordinates (u across the bay between its columns' faces, v up the storey from the floor to the underside of the beam above): its members ({from, to, section}) and glazing ([u0, v0, u1, v1] panes); a frame's own 'modules' add to or replace these.  A panel code joins modules with '+'.", "The rarity emblem is three folded blades a third of a turn apart round its centre, pointing the emblem rightwards: each blade a lit face ('light') and a shaded one ('shade', drawn at 'shade_opacity' of the emblem's ink), corners in units of the emblem's width (x right, y up), measured off the reference's emblems."],
